  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting the Resources**\n\nI\'ve just finished reviewing the resources. The mockups specify `Hanken Grotesk` and `JetBrains Mono` from Google Fonts, and `Material Symbols Outlined` are imported. `Lucide React` is also being used.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Specifications**\n\nI\'ve examined the color palette, noting the base, surfaces, primary, secondary, warning, and error colors. The metadata confirms the project\'s name is \"Argus Criminal Intelligence Platform.\" I\'m also considering the use of an Express server with Vite middleware to incorporate Gemini AI Copilot functionality. Finally, I\'ve checked the scripts in `package.json`.\n\n\n**Reviewing the API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the API endpoints. I see the server is set up to run from `dist/server.cjs`, using Node.js. It will have `/api/copilot/chat`, `/api/copilot/analyze-entity`, and `/api/copilot/subpoena` powered by Gemini AI, with a fallback to local forensic models in case of API or network issues.\n\n\n**Examining the Core Data**\n\nThe initial overview is coming together, featuring a progress gauge at 68%. Key entities are clearly defined, including Rahul Sharma and Aegis Holdings. I am also working on the recent activity feed, which tracks important events like entity links, large transactions, and compliance breaches.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Unpacking the Risks**\n\nMy focus is now on the technical assessment. A HIGH RISK alert, T-8812, has been identified, and I am assessing the confidence interval and suggested actions. I\'m also incorporating an \'Active Alerts\' section highlighting a critical alert about a bridge entity, which requires further investigation.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Alerts**\n\nI am now delving into the recently surfaced alerts. Specifically, I am analyzing a cross-case recurrence involving a phone number that has come up in multiple active cases. I\'m also examining a suspicious financial anomaly: a circular transaction detected within CN-2026-0142. My analysis includes assessing these risks, as well as incorporating the \"Active Alerts\" section. I have also begun reviewing the AI Copilot Panel and Network Intelligence features. I\'m examining the node graph and Forensic Dossier sidebar details for deeper analysis.\n\n\n**Developing the Core Views**\n\nI\'m now implementing the main navigation views in detail. I\'m focusing on the INTELLIGENCE view, which will feature a pattern match matrix, anomaly detection, predictive link scoring, and syndicate clustering. I\'m also planning the EVIDENCE locker with file previews and hash verification. Lastly, I\'m integrating interactive forensic timelines. The goal is to provide rich depth for each core view.\n\n\n**Defining the Structure**\n\nNow, I\'m defining core app components. Specifically, I am planning modular components and types to structure the application. I\'ll include components for comprehensive intelligence report generators, and for case selection modals that permit switching between different investigations. I\'m incorporating a diagnostic modal to display real-time telemetry and a dedicated profile settings section. I am preparing the `metadata.json`, `index.html`, `server.ts` and `package.json` files for modification.\n\n\n**Outlining the Components**\n\nMy current focus is on defining core components. I\'ve broken down specific files: `index.ts` models for data like cases and entities; mock data for rich intelligence; the sidebar with its styling and AI trigger; and the header with indicators. I\'ve also detailed three views: the Command Center with its live trace; Case Investigation with tabs and gauges; and Network Intelligence with its interactive canvas and dossier.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 885789136
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
